  <div class="container">

    <section id="about">
      <h2>About Me</h2>
      <p>Liyema Mahleza is an aspiring Cybersecurity Analyst and Information Security Specialist, completing her BSocSci degree at the University of Cape Town alongside the ALX Cybersecurity programme.</p>
      <p>She is deeply passionate about the <strong>Healthcare GCGO</strong>, believing that protecting digital systems in healthcare is essential for safeguarding patient data, ensuring equitable access to care, and building resilient societies. Her goal is to bridge technology and healthcare by securing hospitals, clinics, and digital health platforms against evolving cyber threats.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="skills">
      <h2>Technical Skills</h2>
      <div class="skills">
        <span class="skill-tag">Data Protection & Compliance</span>
        <span class="skill-tag">Technical Troubleshooting</span>
        <span class="skill-tag">Product Management</span>
        <span class="skill-tag">Incident Handling</span>
        <span class="skill-tag">CRM Systems</span>
        <span class="skill-tag">Analytical Thinking</span>
        <span class="skill-tag">Technical Communication</span>
        <span class="skill-tag">Fast System Learning</span>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="projects">
      <h2>Key Projects</h2>
      <div class="project">
        <h3>Team Jasiri Mama Safe Africa Mobile App</h3>
        <p><strong>Product Manager</strong> — Led product development, feature prioritization, and ensured secure data practices for a safety-focused mobile application.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="project">
        <h3>ALX Cybersecurity Programme</h3>
        <p>Hands-on labs and projects covering security fundamentals, threat identification, and basic incident response.</p>
      </div>
